  "criteria": "For each FSx ONTAP file system, evaluate real configuration (do not assume) against the following checklist. Mark each as PASS or FAIL with a one-line reason, and note severity (high/medium/low) for failures.\n\nBACKUP:\n- Automatic daily backups enabled (automatic_backup_retention_days > 0)\n- Backup retention period >= 7 days (recommended minimum)\n- Daily automatic backup start time configured outside peak usage hours (flag if default/unverified)\n- Volume-level snapshot policies configured (not 'none') on each volume\n- SnapMirror or cross-region/cross-account DR replication configured for production-tier volumes, if applicable\n\nOBSERVABILITY:\n- CloudWatch alarms exist for storage capacity utilization (e.g. nearing SSD/aggregate capacity)\n- CloudWatch alarms exist for throughput/IOPS utilization or throttling\n- Audit logging enabled for CIFS/NFS access where applicable\n- Any EventBridge/notification configuration for FSx lifecycle or health events\n\nOPERATIONS:\n- Weekly maintenance window is explicitly configured (not left to default without review)\n- Deployment type is Multi-AZ (HA) for anything that looks like a production workload (infer from naming/tags); flag Single-AZ as fail with medium/high severity depending on tags\n- Storage capacity headroom: flag if used capacity is approaching provisioned capacity (e.g. >80%)\n- Resources are tagged consistently (owner/environment tags present)\n- SVM and Active Directory join status is healthy (not MISCONFIGURED/FAILED)\n\nPERFORMANCE:\n- Throughput capacity tier appears sized for observed throughput (check CloudWatch for sustained throughput near provisioned ceiling)\n- IOPS mode (automatic vs user-provisioned) and whether observed IOPS approach any provisioned ceiling\n- Tiering policy configured appropriately (e.g. AUTO/SNAPSHOT_ONLY/ALL vs NONE) and consistent with cost/performance intent\n- No sustained high latency indicated in available CloudWatch metrics\n\nSECURITY:\n- Encryption at rest enabled with KMS key (note if AWS-managed vs CMK)\n- In-transit encryption / Kerberos (NFS) or SMB encryption enabled where supported\n- Network exposure: file system subnets/security groups restrict access appropriately (no overly permissive 0.0.0.0/0 ingress)\n- Volume security style (UNIX/NTFS/MIXED) matches intended protocol usage\n- Active Directory / SVM admin access follows least privilege (cannot fully verify IAM/AD internals — note as informational if not verifiable)\n\nReturn a clear per-file-system table or list with pillar groupings, pass/fail per check with a short reason, and overall severity-ranked summary of failures across all file systems."
}", "deep_research": true}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Gather FSx for NetApp ONTAP config and CloudWatch data for a best-practices pass/fail review."}], "created_at": null}

